pve-meta-traefik (0.1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The cluster token needs VM.Audit and nothing else since pve-meta 0.2:
    the permission-file section is gone. Verified end-to-end on the lab:
    a Host() router with a port renders the guest's address from the
    cluster, routes, and 404s anything unmatched.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:00:00 +0200

pve-meta-traefik (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Container image: ghcr.io/arki05/pve-meta-traefik, a static binary on
    scratch, amd64 and arm64, built and pushed by CI on every tag.
  * The service is restarted on package upgrade; --no-start had suppressed
    the restart and left it stopped.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:30:00 +0200

pve-meta-traefik (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `port` (and `scheme`) on a router builds the router's service: one server
    on that port at the guest's address, named after the router or after the
    router's `service`. A name also declared under `services` is refused.
  * README: the Traefik-side defaults (an `asDefault` entry point with a TLS
    block, a middleware chain in the file provider) that keep documents short.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +0200

